================================================================================
1. THE WORK
================================================================================

This repository contains the source of myobservatory.org: the Sky Atlas, FOV
Viewer, Sky Conditions Planner, Astro Calculators, Sampling Calculator, My Gear
and the gallery site around them, together with the astrophotographs they
display.

All of it -- the source code, the page designs, the written text, and every
photograph in images/ -- is the exclusive property of Washington Valley
Observatory and is protected by copyright.

================================================================================
2. WHAT IS NOT PERMITTED
================================================================================

No licence is granted, expressly or by implication, to any person obtaining a
copy of this material. In particular, you may NOT:

  (a) copy, reproduce or republish this source, in whole or in part;
  (b) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works from it;
  (c) distribute, sublicense, sell, rent or lease it;
  (d) host it, or any substantial part of it, on any other domain or service;
  (e) reuse the photographs in images/ for any purpose, commercial or
      otherwise, including as training data for machine-learning systems;
  (f) remove or alter any copyright notice it carries.

This applies whether the material was obtained from this repository, from the
published website, or from a browser cache -- the fact that a web browser must
download this code in order to run it does not place it in the public domain
and grants no licence to reuse it.

================================================================================
3. WHAT IS PERMITTED
================================================================================

You may use the published website at myobservatory.org for its intended
purpose: planning and carrying out your own astronomical observations. Output
you generate with these tools -- framing exports, share links, calculator
results -- is yours to use freely, including commercially.

Viewing the source in a browser's developer tools, for your own private study,
is neither prevented nor objected to. Reproducing it is what is reserved.

